NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/delegate.Client.Run kind=method
  digest=b3:3bbc4d1a4a4eba948de0cc9ed4562571c12ac6aa1dc4ec7e08d1516eaa20e801 file=neo/internal/delegate/client.go range=130:158 lang=go exported=true byte_range=4568:6046
  sig=func (c *Client) Run(ctx context.Context, prose string) (string, error)
  doc=Run submits the intent and blocks until it terminates, servicing approval\ngates inline (via track). On a deterministic-id conflict (a 409 "already\nexists in async registry") it does NOT fail or re-submit: the work is\nalready in flight, so it ATTACHES to the existing intent and tracks it to\nits terminal outcome (or returns that outcome directly if it is already\nterminal). Returns the deliverable answer, or an error describing the\nfailure / clarification needed / timeout (which the model relays).
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/delegate.Client
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/delegate/client.go

